# Living Newar/Krama material

## 17. **Kālīkulakramārcana**

This is a Newar Kālīkrama liturgical work by Vimalaprabodha. It survives in several Nepalese manuscripts. Pongsit Pangsrivongse produced an edition as part of his doctoral work, but I found no complete publicly available English translation. ([Springer][16])

## 18. **Parvatrayavidhāna**

This is a previously unknown work by the same Krama author, also edited in Pangsrivongse’s 2023 thesis. It is used in recent research on Newar ritual philosophy but has not appeared as a complete general English translation. ([Springer][16])

### Why these are special

They connect classical Krama theory to the still-living Newar ritual environment:

```text
Kashmiri Krama doctrine
        ↓
Nepalese transmission
        ↓
Newar liturgy
        ↓
philosophical verses embedded in ritual
```

**Recommendation:** collaborator-based project rather than an automated scrape-and-translate target.

